From e44b5d440787e7314721379a0d7027170d53ed14 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 11:58:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] GSTIN statuses ready/verifying, approval in Frappe, and App
 Notifications

- New consent_status values: ready (business has active, verified Adaequare
  Settings) and verifying (OTP verified, waiting for approval).
- Adaequare Settings save checks the credentials with a GSP token
  (credentials_verified) and moves the business's GSTINs inactive <-> ready;
  turning it off or deleting it moves ready back to inactive. GSTINs added
  later start as ready.
- connect/resend refuse inactive GSTINs (outside mock mode) and GSTINs
  waiting for approval. Verify (or no OTP needed) now stops at verifying.
- approve_gstin_connection / reject_gstin_connection (System Manager, not for
  a GST User); buttons on the GSTIN and Adaequare Settings forms; GSTIN list
  indicators and a status filter.
- litwatch/notifications.py notify(): App Notifications for ready, waiting
  for verification (approvers), connected and rejected, sent from
  GSTIN.on_update so each change notifies once.
- Patch gstin_ready_status backfills inactive -> ready without notifications.
- Tests: test_gstin_status (whole flow); scoping test uses the mock portal.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016uSTwic31grtwzMMK7rPAR
